## Just Completed

- 2026-08-03: Discovered and fully specified a **critical post-release bug**: every himalaya-mcp
  MCP tool call fails against `himalaya 2.0.0` (Homebrew's current stable) because
  `HimalayaClient.execOnce()` unconditionally sends `--output json`, a flag the v2 CLI rejects
  outright; confirmed live against a real UNM IMAP account (not a config/account issue —
  `--json` returns real inbox data immediately). Root cause, full reproduction transcripts, and
  every broken call site: `docs/specs/BUG-himalaya-v2-cli-incompatibility-2026-08-03.md`.
  Ran full spec-driven-development Phase 1 (Specify) → two adversarial reviews (code-quality +
  security) surfaced 1 CRITICAL + 2 HIGH + 2 MEDIUM findings, all resolved (including a live
  `imap create`/`imap delete` verification against the real account, cleaned up after) — decided
  to support **both** himalaya v1.x and v2.x (not a cutover):
  `docs/specs/SPEC-himalaya-v2-cli-compat-2026-08-03.md`. Phase 2 (Plan) done:
  `tasks/plan.md` + `tasks/todo.md` (9 tasks, T1–T9, dependency-ordered).
- 2026-08-03 (later same day): Implemented T1–T8 in worktree
  `~/.git-worktrees/himalaya-mcp/feature-cli-v2-compat` (branch `feature/himalaya-cli-v2-compat`),
  **uncommitted**. `npm run build` and `npm run build:bundle` both pass clean; a manual (non-vitest)
  smoke script exercised the real compiled code against a CI argv fixture in both v1/v2 modes —
  passed. Found and fixed 3 bugs beyond the original task list (a second broken call site in
  `sendTemplate()`, a third in doctor's `checkEmailConnectivity()` plus two v2 JSON-shape bugs,
  and a version-regex bug caught only by the manual smoke run) — full detail in
  `tasks/todo.md`'s "Follow-ups" section. **T9 (full `npm test` run) not done — needs the user**,
  per the vitest process-leak issue (see Testing note below).
- 2026-08-03: Diagnosed the recurring vitest process-leak (Codex rescue research,
  `feedback_no_vitest_direct.md` in memory) — a harness Bash-timeout/vitest-SIGTERM interaction,
  not a vitest bug or project misconfig. Adopted Docker (bind-mounted worktree + named
  `node_modules` volume, `--rm`) as the standing T9 verification method — leaked fork-pool
  workers die with the container instead of the host.
- 2026-08-03/04: Ran T9 (full suite) via Docker — first pass surfaced 48 failures (fake-himalaya
  E2E fixtures not answering the new `--version` probe), then 25 (mocked `execFileAsync`/`spawn`
  in `retry.test.ts`/`manage.test.ts`/`dogfood-reliability.test.ts`/`client.test.ts` not
  accounting for the extra probe call), then found and fixed 2 real test-fixture bugs: a JS
  `.replace()` pattern-string `$1` collision that corrupted `spawnHarnessWithFakeHimalaya`'s
  version guard, and a `fakeChildProcess()` construction-time-vs-call-time race in the new
  `sendTemplate` spawn tests. Final: 666/666 tests, 36/36 files, exit 0. Full detail in
  `tasks/todo.md` T9. Committed, pushed, PR #118 → `dev` opened.
- 2026-08-04: PR #118's `test` CI check failed on `npm audit --audit-level=high` — 3 pre-existing
  high/moderate transitive-dep vulnerabilities (`fast-uri`, `hono`, `ip-address`), confirmed also
  failing on `dev`'s own latest CI run (not a regression from #118). Fixed in a separate PR #119
  (`npm audit fix`, lockfile-only, 0 vulnerabilities, 619/619 tests via Docker) to keep #118's
  diff clean. Both PRs code-reviewed, CI verified green, merged (squash) to `dev` in order:
